{"availability":"available","full":"solvi-ai/solvi","name":"solvi","description":"A runtime where decision models propose and your code decides: typed questions, hard rules, quotes checked against the text, escalation with a guaranteed error budget, replayable traces. Works with any System One model.","category":"Finance","language":"Python","stars":3,"forks":0,"created":"2026-09-26T10:13:43Z","updated":"2026-10-04T06:43:55Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://solvi-ai.github.io/solvi/","topics":["agent-guardrails","ai-agents","audit-trail","conformal-prediction","decision-making","decision-models","explainable-ai","guardrails","information-extraction","llm","mcp","onnx","provenance","pydantic","python","rules-engine","small-language-models"],"demo":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/solvi-ai/playground","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T20:07:41.192Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T20:07:41.192Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T20:07:41.192Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-04T08:17:22.890Z","stars":1,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-06T16:29:32.332Z","stars":3,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-08T20:07:41.192Z","stars":3,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Decision systems you can check. You describe what to compute with plain Python functions and checks; a model — an LLM, your own classifier or a small local one — proposes where judgement is needed; solvi's checks decide. Every answer comes with a confidence, a reason you can check (the rule's inputs, a formula over computed facts, or a quote with character offsets in the source) and a hash-chained trace that can be re-executed later to confirm the answer or pinpoint the step that was altered. When something cannot be computed or checked, solvi abstains or hands the case to a person instead of…","solvi 1.0 has two levels. Ready systems you configure: solvi.build (decisions from labelled examples, with a promise on the errors), solvi.Agent (acting in an environment), solvi.Guard (an agent's tool calls) and solvi.Knowledge (what they know, and from whom). Building blocks in solvi.core, which the ready systems are made of, each replaceable by a part of your own. What works but has no measured gain yet is kept apart in solvi.experimental."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/solvi-ai/solvi/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"43e522b317a233ea0eaa8fa6f3b07d56d0d1af07c624c362c50c2133eea767d4","extractedAt":"2026-10-04T06:51:14.552Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T06:51:14.552Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Decision systems you can check. You describe what to compute with plain Python functions and checks; a model — an LLM, your own classifier or a small local one — proposes where judgement is needed; solvi's checks decide. Every answer comes with a confidence, a reason you can check (the rule's inputs, a formula over computed facts, or a quote with character offsets in the source) and a hash-chained trace that can be re-executed later to confirm the answer or pinpoint the step that was altered. When something cannot be computed or checked, solvi abstains or hands the case to a person instead of…","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/solvi-ai/solvi/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"paid_service","status":"required","text":"The default strategist needs the inputs of every producer of a fact. solvi.core.plan.cost.CostStrategist() plans around producers whose inputs are never given, and with producers=\"equivalent\" picks the cheapest verified plan by declared cost= (an exact 0/1 program; hard checks that govern a question always stay in the plan).","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/solvi-ai/solvi/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"paid_service","status":"optional","text":"The parts are trivial arithmetic: running all of them (\"run all\") costs less than one ask, so the saving shows only when parts are slow (services, models), as in the insurance desk below.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/solvi-ai/solvi/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"43e522b317a233ea0eaa8fa6f3b07d56d0d1af07c624c362c50c2133eea767d4","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/solvi-ai/solvi/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-04T06:51:14.553Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-04T06:43:55Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/solvi-ai/solvi/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-04T06:51:14.555Z","hash":"43e522b317a233ea0eaa8fa6f3b07d56d0d1af07c624c362c50c2133eea767d4","originalBytes":46705,"storedBytes":46705,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["examples","solvi","model","one","system","docs","answer","what","every","decision","questions","each","text","question","answers","hard","catalog","check","checks","agent","when","llm","per","rules","run","learned","models","over","same","benchmarks","decider","decisions","field","rule","world","ask","code","guard","only","plan","slow","trace","typed","without","import","python","stored","types","approve","cost","does","install","parts","risk","solvi-ai","strategist","guide","inputs","json","labelled","path","tasks","them","alone","audit","confidence","decide","documents","fields","given","own","part","receipts","runs","state","steps","under","verified","vote","which","answered","building","cat","checked","days","def","enough","environment","first","knowledge","mcp","promise","pydantic","quote","reads","replay","res","return","see","several","solvi-base","solvi.build","start","takes","their","ticket","tool","true","two","across","act","after","balance","behind","calls","card","checkpoint","coding","computed","contract","date","description","entry","extract-base","facts","gallery","guarantee","input","needs","person","pip","print","quotes","read","record","says","solvi.agent","systems","task","through","value","values","where","api","catalog.py","contracts","escalates","escalation","extractor","fact","grounded","how","labeled","leave","local","long","model.py","nev